<title>UK: John Menzies Christmas sales below year ago.</title>
<headline>John Menzies Christmas sales below year ago.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>British newsagent chain John Menzies said on Thursday that Christmas sales were &quot;just below&quot; last year and warned this performance, together with a shortfall in half year profits, would not be made up in the year.</p>
<p>It said pretax profits for the six months ending November 2 were 2.6 million stg, down from 3.8 million stg a year ago, but paid out an unchanged dividend of 4.8 pence per share.</p>
